WEBVTT

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.530
The genius from the 
darkness, Akagi Shigeru.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:19.070
Washizu Iwao, the monster 
of the Showa Era.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.130
The Washizu Mahjong deathmatch

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.690
with both of their demises 
on the line continues.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:27.970
Akagi managed to take the 
lead in the first and second

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:29.520
matches by outwitting Washizu.

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:32.080
Washizu is being backed into a corner.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.670
However, he puts his pride as the 
king who ruled from the shadows

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:37.170
on the line and stays in the fight.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.950
Now the third match has begun.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.140
A new battle is about to commence.

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:48.730
<b>Episode 23</b>

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:48.730
<b>The Power of Brute Luck</b>

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:53.020
Akagi has lost 1,100 CCs 
of blood thus far.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.840
He has only 900 CCs left before death.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.950
He's on his last legs.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.690
<i>I'll finish him.</i>

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:19.520
<i>Destroying this man would be a 
fitting end to my reign in Japan.</i>

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:25.640
<i>If possible, I want to 
win by outranking him.</i>

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.420
<i>These high stakes led to 
very special conditions,</i>

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.420
<i>and those in turn created 
this special situation.</i>

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.170
<i>I don't want to use tricks to defeat him,</i>

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.170
<i>but crush him with my skills alone.</i>

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.170
<i>That will truly prove my superiority.</i>

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.410
<i>I will end you.</i>

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:48.950
However...

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:50.580
Tsumo.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.650
Tsumo, ittsuu, three dora.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:02.660
Haneman.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.450
Akagi strikes first.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.010
By continuously discarding 
what is unnecessary,

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:13.670
he ends up with an ideal hand.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.680
It is the type of ideal 
win that only comes when

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.190
the flow of the game favors you.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.670
He pulls away from Washizu.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.650
Don't get cocky, boy.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.910
We're just getting started.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.430
It's only East Hand 1.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.390
The fight is just starting.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.140
<i>No.</i>

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.860
<i>This could get rough.</i>

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:47.100
<i>Based on what we've seen so far, 
we have to admit that this man</i>

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.050
<i>might be one grade higher 
than Washizu-sama.</i>

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:56.080
<i>He is like a demon.</i>

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.340
<i>And now the luck seems entirely 
with him this third match.</i>

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.850
<i>Unless something big happens...</i>

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.580
<i>we'll lose!</i>

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:12.350
Should Washizu waste his chance 
as dealer here in East Hand 2,

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.020
the game will most likely go to Akagi.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:20.060
He must win, even with 
a 1,500 or 2,000 hand.

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:24.780
It is crucial for Washizu to turn 
the flow of the game around.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:28.660
But Akagi won East Hand 1.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.570
The game is favoring him even more.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.160
Washizu is in a bad position.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.580
Just as everybody was thinking 
that his hand is sinking,

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:39.080
that it can only go down...

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:42.580
An auspicious turn.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.090
Could this be Washizu's magic?

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:48.790
He has no melds,

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:52.090
but he is 3 tiles away from a 
possible tanpin, sanshoku hand.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.200
<i>Not bad.</i>

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.050
<i>He could fight back with this.</i>

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:02.690
<i>The problem is Akagi's hand.</i>

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:06.630
<i>He has four black tiles.</i>

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:10.180
<i>I can't be too certain, but from 
what I can see, it's not good.</i>

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.480
<i>There's some hope.</i>

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:13.550
<i>And yet...</i>

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.420
<i>Washizu-sama's born aptitude,</i>

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.650
<i>his power,</i>

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:20.390
<i>the strength of his luck...</i>

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:24.840
<i>Ordinary standards can't 
measure how good his luck is.</i>

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.640
<i>No matter how many 
times his back comes</i>

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.900
<i>up against the wall, 
he comes out alive.</i>

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:34.420
<i>He is the type who will overcome 
the worst odds to come out on top.</i>

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.470
<i>The same was true for the 
recent vampire murders.</i>

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:44.160
<i>Even though he had to 
sacrifice much of his fortune,</i>

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:47.380
<i>he survived despite having 
committed those atrocities.</i>

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:52.490
<i>This man will always survive.</i>

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:55.490
<i>If you consider that...</i>

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:58.220
<i>there is still a chance we may win.</i>

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:04.460
<i>Akagi may be a better player, 
but Washizu-sama has better luck.</i>

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.210
<i>And with that luck, 
bestowed by the heavens,</i>

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.340
<i>he can bring Akagi to his knees.</i>

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:12.940
<i>He has a chance at victory!</i>

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:17.170
As if to confirm Yoshioka's thoughts, 
Washizu draws a 9 of bamboo,

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:19.910
which puts him two tiles from tenpai.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.650
But he loses the chance to get 
a tanpin, sanshoku, tanyao.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:27.540
<i>That's fine.</i>

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.650
<i>Right now, that is fine.</i>

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:31.970
<i>Speed is of the essence.</i>

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:34.390
<i>More than anything, he needs 
to focus on staying dealer.</i>

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.710
But in the next turn...

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:43.630
He loses his chance 
at a pinfu because his

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.100
2 of bamboo pair turns into a triplet.

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.900
Though his hand is progressing, 
it's doing so in the worst way.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:52.340
His hand becomes increasingly cheaper.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:55.950
This just confirms that 
Washizu is in a bad position.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:06:59.110
In a normal situation,

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:02.850
useless draws at this point in the 
game would be par for the course.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:07.360
But right now, 
Washizu is forcing these tiles.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:13.130
He is like a writhing dragon 
ascending into the stormy sky.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:22.160
A dragon who climbs through 
the sky amidst violent winds.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:26.120
And yet, no matter how 
strong this dragon may be,

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:31.220
if it tries to force its way 
upward against fierce headwinds,

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.910
it will exhaust its strength and weaken...

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:38.110
and eventually fall.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:40.360
Even if...

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.600
it's the monster called Washizu.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:50.500
<i>Now the sanshoku is gone, too.</i>

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:52.340
<i>It's a completely worthless hand.</i>

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:55.620
<i>But right now, 
he needs to get into tenpai.</i>

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.730
<i>He has a two-sided wait.</i>

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:01.520
<i>Should he get the dora, the 6 of 
circles, instead of the 9 of circles,</i>

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:03.110
<i>it will be a riichi, ippatsu, with one dora.</i>

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:06.850
<i>With any reverse dora, 
it could even be a mangan.</i>

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:11.320
However,

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.320
even that is gone.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:19.860
Everything drawn cheapened his hand.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:23.720
The potential for the mentanpin, 
sanshoku is gone without a trace.

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:26.330
<i>At least he's in tenpai.</i>

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:30.510
<i>And with this single wait 
on the 1 of circles...</i>

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:34.170
<i>Suzuki can deal into his hand right away.</i>

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:37.080
<i>At least he can win.</i>

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:41.580
At this time, Washizu delays 
calling a riichi for one turn.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:45.090
This is because Suzuki 
could declare a kan.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:49.780
It's not too late to declare riichi 
after Suzuki's kan reveals the new dora.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:51.430
Kan.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:57.460
In the current situation, he can't 
expect miracles from the new dora.

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:59.830
The flow of the entire game is against him.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:03.920
Everyone is thinking along those 
lines for this concealed kan.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.030
And yet...

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:21.050
<i>It's a...</i>

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:22.570
1 of bamboo!

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:24.560
So the new dora is the 2 of bamboo?

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:28.020
That means Washizu has...

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:29.760
three dora!

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:31.500
Three dora!

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:33.390
Three dora!

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.380
An unexpected development.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:46.260
Despite fighting an uphill battle,

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:48.380
Washizu gets three dora from 
the new dora indicator.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:51.150
Usually something like 
this does not happen.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:56.740
<i>This is how strong Washizu-sama's luck is.</i>

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:59.360
<i>This is what he was born with.</i>

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:04.740
<i>No, it surpasses even that... 
This is brute luck.</i>

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:28.820
Riichi.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.890
<i>That's it.</i>

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:43.140
<i>He's got a dealer mangan in the bag now.</i>

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:46.510
<i>Now Suzuki just has to deal 
the 1 of circles into his hand.</i>

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:48.860
Riichi, ippatsu, three dora.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:52.510
If he gets any reverse dora, 
it'll be a haneman or even a baiman.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:56.260
Washizu gets a hand that 
can cause an instant upset.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:11:00.480
<i>He can defeat Akagi!</i>

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:15.360
<i>What?</i>

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.470
<i>The 2 of characters?</i>

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:18.290
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:21.550
<i>Why didn't he deal that 
1 of circles into his hand?</i>

00:11:22.270 --> 00:11:26.210
<i>The 1 of circles we need 
for the dealer mangan...</i>

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:33.790
<i>I get it!</i>

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:36.470
<i>Akagi has a 1 of circles.</i>

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:42.220
<i>And it looks like both the 1 and 
3 of circles are useless to him.</i>

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:45.960
<i>So he'll be discarding those because...</i>

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.750
<i>Suzuki already has a 
triplet of the 2 of circles</i>

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.010
<i>he needs to complete that sequence.</i>

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:56.200
<i>It's hard for him to complete the 
sequence and it's a bad wait, too.</i>

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:58.940
<i>It's a closed wait he 
must want to get rid of.</i>

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:02.680
<i>The 3 of circles is already a 
safe tile with Washizu-sama.</i>

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:06.190
<i>And since Washizu-sama 
didn't have Suzuki deal</i>

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:08.680
<i>the 1 of circles into his hand just now,</i>

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:13.190
<i>Akagi most likely thinks it'll pass, as well.</i>

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.270
If one assumes that

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:18.690
Suzuki's tiles do not contain the 
winning tile, but only safe tiles,

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:24.700
the logic of the second 
discard pile is established.

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:29.940
Washizu set up a trap 
by using that logic.

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:33.410
<i>He added it to his hand!</i>

00:12:34.990 --> 00:12:41.380
<i>If Akagi discards the 1 of circles... 
he'll lose 1,200 CCs.</i>

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:47.460
<i>With the 1,100 CCs he already 
lost, that'll be 2,300 CCs.</i>

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:49.950
<i>That's nearly half of 
what a human body holds.</i>

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:52.370
<i>Of course he won't survive that.</i>

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:53.420
<i>He'll die!</i>

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:56.380
<i>He simply can't survive!</i>

00:12:57.410 --> 00:13:00.330
It's a veritable discard of death.

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:02.430
<i>If it's the 1 of circles, it's...</i>

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:04.440
<i>Death!</i>

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:22.540
<i>Of course.</i>

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:24.990
<i>He would figure this one out.</i>

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:28.730
<i>He can see through this kind of trap.</i>

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:32.010
<i>That's to be expected of this kid.</i>

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:37.560
<i>His senses are extraordinary and 
far surpass those of normal people.</i>

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:41.070
<i>But here, that's just fine.</i>

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:43.050
<i>If I always stick to the formula</i>

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:45.730
<i>of riichi followed by my winning 
tile being discarded instantly,</i>

00:13:45.730 --> 00:13:47.650
<i>the only thing I can gain is points.</i>

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:49.750
<i>There's never anything on top.</i>

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:53.980
<i>And that's no fun.</i>

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:57.490
<i>That won't breed any fear.</i>

00:13:57.990 --> 00:14:00.220
<i>I am going to stick with this trap.</i>

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:03.990
<i>It'll be fun to sow the seed of suspicion.</i>

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:07.730
<i>Even if it's an obvious trap,</i>

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:11.530
<i>I'll deliberately sow the seed of suspicion.</i>

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:17.230
<i>Instead of the usual routine of riichi 
followed by my winning tile,</i>

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:20.820
<i>I'll wait one turn for 
seemingly no reason.</i>

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:24.800
<i>It'll be fun to see what he'll 
make of the new pattern.</i>

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:28.210
<i>In other words, he'll be shaken.</i>

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:33.860
<i>I'm going to shake your confidence 
in that second discard pile.</i>

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:38.090
<i>That'll show its effects later.</i>

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:40.600
<i>In a heavier,</i>

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:42.830
<i>heavier,</i>

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:46.070
<i>heavier scene.</i>

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.980
<i>The second discard pile you took 
advantage of will breed doubt.</i>

00:14:50.980 --> 00:14:56.500
<i>You thought you were smart, but soon 
you will drown in your own cleverness.</i>

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:02.130
Washizu's first draw after his riichi.

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:05.820
If he gets the ippatsu here, 
he will have a haneman hand.

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:09.860
He'll get 6,000 from everybody and 
Akagi will lose 600 CCs of blood.

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:13.830
A total of 1,700 CCs, an amount 
that could easily be fatal.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:20.070
<i>If I draw it, you will die.</i>

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:25.310
<i>If this is the 1 of circles...</i>

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.230
<i>Die!</i>

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:45.990
He's right. If that had been the 1 
of circles, Akagi would have died.

00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:53.470
With no recourse, with no way of 
defending himself, Akagi would have died.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.580
<i>That's right.</i>

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:01.470
<i>Why was I in such a rush?</i>

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:07.980
<i>I lost my composure just because 
I lost the first two matches</i>

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.450
<i>and because I let him take 
an early lead in the third.</i>

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:14.720
<i>It's stupid to even feel 
like I've been cornered.</i>

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:18.460
<i>I am the one with the 
utmost advantage here.</i>

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:24.200
<i>He should be the one who's shaking.</i>

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:26.430
<i>He kept that one.</i>

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:32.440
<i>If I draw it, he'll either die instantly or be on the verge of dying.</i>

00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:37.940
<i>If he were to deal into my hand, 
he'd die without question.</i>

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:41.450
<i>He'll dry out and die.</i>

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:45.650
<i>All he'll have left to do 
is die a pathetic death.</i>

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:55.430
<i>That's right.</i>

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:57.060
<i>It's the opposite.</i>

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:59.810
<i>The exact opposite.</i>

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:05.400
<i>He's the one who's being 
cornered and pressured.</i>

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:08.410
<i>He's the one who's struggling.</i>

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:11.800
Indeed, by merely getting into a tenpai

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:15.720
with a haneman hand, Washizu can 
decisively corner his opponents.

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:19.420
That doesn't apply to just Akagi.

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.660
<i>That's right, be afraid.</i>

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:32.960
<i>I'm the one on the higher ground!</i>

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:36.780
<i>Even if I missed the ippatsu,</i>

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:40.130
<i>one reverse dora will be 
enough for a haneman.</i>

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:43.170
<i>The haneman that'll bring death to Akagi.</i>

00:17:43.630 --> 00:17:46.680
<i>Meaning this is the draw that'll kill him.</i>

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:48.920
<i>The draw that'll kill him.</i>

00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:53.920
<i>The draw that'll kill him.</i>

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:18.910
<i>Washizu-sama, what should I do?</i>

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.450
<i>Should I discard this?</i>

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:23.140
<i>No no. Why rush?</i>

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:26.880
<i>Let me have more fun.</i>

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:29.940
<i>I can win at any time.</i>

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:33.390
<i>Take a good look at their hands.</i>

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:36.490
<i>That cop's hand is nowhere.</i>

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:38.890
<i>That pair of red dragons could be key,</i>

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:41.310
<i>but unless he can turn it into a triplet,</i>

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:43.400
<i>he'll take ages to get into tenpai.</i>

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:50.610
<i>And Akagi is... two away from tenpai, at best.</i>

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:52.410
<i>He's out, too!</i>

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:56.100
Since Suzuki has three of the 2 of circles,

00:18:56.100 --> 00:19:00.410
Akagi would have to wait for the last 
2 of circles, even if he was in tenpai.

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:02.410
<i>We'll keep going.</i>

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:03.420
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:09.160
<i>We still have a lot of time to spare.</i>

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:11.550
That same turn, Akagi...

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:19.630
<i>Fun! How fun!</i>

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:22.370
<i>This is really fun.</i>

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:25.600
<i>Now the 3 of circles has become his pair.</i>

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:28.340
<i>So the 1 of circles is isolated now.</i>

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:32.340
<i>Which means that maybe...</i>

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:38.320
<i>Will it come out?</i>

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:45.170
<i>So you won't discard it after all?</i>

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:49.000
<i>I suppose you still have 
more unnecessary tiles.</i>

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:53.320
<i>But this man probably knows.</i>

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:56.030
<i>That he can't discard that 1 of circles.</i>

00:19:56.030 --> 00:20:04.980
<i>I'm sure that he knows that the 
1 of circles in Suzuki's hand is my trap.</i>

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:10.510
<i>Oh, well.</i>

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:17.250
<i>It doesn't matter how well 
you can read our hands.</i>

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:22.120
<i>If I draw it here, that's it.</i>

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:24.940
<i>Everything will be over.</i>

00:20:27.130 --> 00:20:28.360
<i>That's right.</i>

00:20:28.630 --> 00:20:33.570
<i>If I draw it now, it'll be done.</i>

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.810
<i>The 1 of circles!</i>

00:20:36.740 --> 00:20:38.540
<i>If I draw it, I can kill him.</i>

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:41.040
<i>The 1 of circles!</i>

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:45.980
<i>If I draw it, I can kill this man!</i>

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:49.050
Death is already standing behind Akagi.

00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:52.340
This is East Hand 2 of the fatal third match.

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:56.400
The monster Washizu with his brute luck...

00:20:57.550 --> 00:20:59.630
What does he have in his grasp?

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:03.390
Is it Akagi's death sentence?

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:05.500
Or is it...

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:18.930
Next time, "The Will of the Demon."

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:20.550
<b>The Will of the Demon</b>
